A||||3||DecadenceR||3 qt or 4 qt???||||1||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||06-30-2001||03:35 PM||||Okay I have an 84 4-banger.<BR>Am I suppoed to put 3 quarts of oil in, or 4???<BR>I seem to remember puting 4 in my old 87. When i had the oil changed at a shop they put in 3, and the haynes manual says 3. This seems low to me.||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||06-30-2001||04:34 PM||||Engine oil capacity:<BR>Page 28 of my haynes manual, 1st page of chapter 1 says 4 qts. factory sticker under decklid also says 4 qts. seems if you put in only 3 qts, dipstick would read low. The only place I see 3 qts is for 84-86 manual transaxle capcity<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 06-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||06-30-2001||04:59 PM||||The original 84's used 3 quarts of oil in the engine.  One of the early recalls changed the capacity to 4 quarts.  The only thing that was changed on the engine was the dipstick! (There was a change in oil filter part number, but the difference in size doesn't come close to another quart.) When you change your oil, put 3 quarts in, run the engine for a few minutes and shut it off.  Check the level on the stick.  If it reads "full", then the recall wasn't done.  If it shows a quart low then add one.  Or just use 4 quarts anyway and don't worry about the stick showing overfull.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||06-30-2001||05:13 PM||||Rod,Thanks for correcting me. I didn't know about the early mdls.<BR>Don <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
